  "confidence": 0.84,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.1", "U15.2", "U15.4", "U22.1", "U22.2", "U22.4", "U35.1", "U35.2", "U35.4", "U36.1", "U36.2", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_SINK1", "ESTOP_SINK2", "ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL", "ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP", "ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(U15-A)", "Net-(U15-Y)"],
      "observed": "The four e-stop buffer components are valued SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, but their MPN fields specify U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R. The netlist assigns them /OE, A, and Y pins, and uses their outputs in the e-stop signal chain.",
      "expected": "The specification identifies these e-stop devices as SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffers used as controlled sinks. The sourced component should match that type and function; the listed 1G125 is a tri-state push-pull buffer, not an open-drain sink.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U15\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"ESTOP_OUT\") ... (node (ref \"U36\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the BOM MPN is used for assembly, the e-stop chain will use push-pull rather than open-drain outputs. This can change the intended sink behavior and may actively drive shared e-stop signals instead of only pulling them low, risking incorrect or unreliable e-stop operation.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The e-stop buffer value and sourcing MPN identify different logic families with materially different output behavior. Because these parts form the specified controlled-sink e-stop chain, the sourcing mismatch could alter a safety-related function."
}

